In React Native, use built-in components like `Text` and `View`.

```jsx
import { Text, View } from 'react-native';

export default function App() {
  return (
    <View>
      <Text>Hello from React Native!</Text>
    </View>
  );
}
```

Functional components are JavaScript functions that return JSX.

```jsx
function Welcome() {
  return <Text>Welcome to React Native</Text>;
}

export default Welcome;
```

Props allow you to pass data from one component to another.

```jsx
function Greeting(props) {
  return <Text>Hello, {props.name}!</Text>;
}

<Greeting name="Alice" />
```

You can set default values for props.

```jsx
Greeting.defaultProps = {
  name: 'Guest'
};
```

Use `prop-types` library to validate the types of props.

```jsx
import PropTypes from 'prop-types';

Greeting.propTypes = {
  name: PropTypes.string
};
```
